    {
      "text": "Most people think coding agents only write code. But if you ask me, that's just bad marketing.",
      "timestamp_sec": 7,
      "why": "Frames the talk's central reframing of what coding agents are for."
    },
    {
      "text": "You have to be able to think like an agent to get it to do what you want it to do.",
      "timestamp_sec": 7,
      "why": "States the thesis in one line, before any of the HTML specifics."
    },
    {
      "text": "Every day, the world pours something like 34,000 human years into making slide decks. Most of that time isn't the thinking, it's the fiddling.",
      "timestamp_sec": 53,
      "why": "The only hard number in the talk, and it sizes the problem."
    },
    {
      "text": "A deck that takes 10 hours should really take about 25 minutes once you remove all the formatting and the branding and the moving things around.",
      "timestamp_sec": 53,
      "why": "Quantifies the claimed upside of removing manual formatting work."
    },
    {
      "text": "Every one of these tools is built for human hands and human eyes.",
