    {
      "text": "If you ask me, it's not the model, it's the medium.",
      "timestamp_sec": 140,
      "why": "The talk's core claim, stated as a direct rebuttal to the skeptic position."
    },
    {
      "text": "If I asked you, someone who is presumably human, to handwrite an SVG of a pelican, you wouldn't be able to do that either.",
      "timestamp_sec": 140,
      "why": "The argument that invalidates the pelican benchmark as a capability test."
    },
    {
      "text": "Asking an AI to use a canvas is like asking a human to write SVG by hand. It doesn't really make sense.",
      "timestamp_sec": 177,
      "why": "The talk's key analogy, inverted to indict the whole class of agent design tools."
    },
    {
      "text": "You need to give the AI tools based on how it thinks, not in pixels, in language. Words, tokens, structure, that is its native medium.",
      "timestamp_sec": 177,
      "why": "Generalizes the argument from graphics to agent tool design broadly."
    },
    {
      "text": "HTML lets the model think in structure. HTML tags have meanings built into the language.",
      "timestamp_sec": 219,
      "why": "The mechanism behind why HTML beats SVG for models."
    },
    {
      "text": "So, the model never actually places a coordinate, and you can get all sorts of visual effects, charts and layouts, fonts and motion, all of it for free.",
      "timestamp_sec": 219,
      "why": "Explains what the browser absorbs on the model's behalf."
    },
    {
      "text": "PowerPoint is a tool that you use to make slide decks. The deck itself, that's just the presentation mode.",
      "timestamp_sec": 268,
      "why": "Separates editing format from output format, which licenses the whole approach."
    },
    {
      "text": "The editing format is totally arbitrary.",
      "timestamp_sec": 268,
      "why": "The pivotal permission-granting claim of the talk."
    },
    {
      "text": "What you're watching is just HTML and CSS. It's literally just divs all the way down.",
      "timestamp_sec": 307,
      "why": "Self-demonstrating evidence — the talk video itself is the artifact."
    },
    {
      "text": "Plain text is a choice, generally a choice of convenience, but it's usually the wrong one if you're actually trying to create something of use.",
      "timestamp_sec": 307,
      "why": "A contrarian take on agent output defaults that extends beyond slides."
    },
    {
      "text": "I do want to take a quick beat here and point out that a beautiful deck on its own is generally not worth anything.",
      "timestamp_sec": 350,
      "why": "Honest caveat that formatting is the smaller half of the problem."
